        "code": {
          "text": "Chronic right lateral epicondylitis, work aggravated"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-1",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-1",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Right elbow pain"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Intermittent, persistent outer right elbow pain for about 9–10 months, worse over the last 2–3 months. Local ache with sharp pain on lifting and gripping. Worse with scanning groceries, lifting bags, pouring a kettle, and gripping a steering wheel, especially with the forearm pronated. Improved with rest and ibuprofen as needed. Occasional night pain when rolling onto that side, waking the patient a few times per week. Mild morning stiffness that settles quickly. Pain increases on long, busy checkout shifts; patient swaps hands and takes brief breaks, and avoids heavy housework and gardening. Activities of daily living remain okay."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-2",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-2",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Subjective right grip strength and function"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Patient reports slightly reduced grip and occasionally drops heavier items. No true weakness; weakness is described as pain limited."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-3",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-3",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Right elbow examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "No deformity or visible swelling. Local tenderness over the right lateral epicondyle/common extensor origin. No medial epicondyle or olecranon tenderness and no warmth. Full flexion, extension, pronation, and supination. Pain reproduced on resisted wrist extension with the elbow extended and forearm pronated, and on resisted middle-finger extension. Right grip slightly reduced compared with left due to pain."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-4",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-4",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Neurologic, vascular, and cervical screen"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Neurovascularly intact with radial pulse present. No cubital tunnel Tinel sign. Brief cervical screen normal. Patient reports no neck pain or paraesthesia."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-5",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-5",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Reported associated symptoms and red flags"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "No trauma, locking, giving way, redness, warmth, or obvious swelling reported. No weight loss, fever, or night sweats. No other joint pain, morning stiffness lasting more than 30 minutes, rash, or psoriasis."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-6",
